      "content": "I see. But couldn't you argue that without secure borders and strict enforcement, the sheer volume of undocumented arrivals could actually destabilize social services and strain the economy in the short-to-medium term? It seems like the enforcement side is more about maintaining the rule of law and national security, which are also fundamental to stability. Why wouldn't that be considered a more \"realistic\" foundation for a long-term solution?",
